<title>PORTUGAL: Foreign investors drive up BTA.</title>
<headline>Foreign investors drive up BTA.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Buy orders from foreign investors drove up shares in Portuguese bank Banto Totta &amp; Acores (BTA) on Lisbon bourse, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Interest in BTA is due to foreign buy orders,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>Another operator said: &quot;It seems that BTA will rise further. At present levels it is still cheap.&quot;</p>
<p>BTA stood at 2,750 escudos, up 17, in high volume of 240,581 shares at 1512 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
